==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|ráð}} from the Old Norse verb {{m|non|ráða}} (Icelandic {{m|is|ráða}}, Swedish {{m|sv|råda}}, Danish {{m|da|råde}}); ultimately from from {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*rēdaną}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*rei-||reason, count}}. Cognate with Old Frisian {{m|ofs|rēda}} (West Frisian {{m|fy|riede}}), Old English {{m|ang|rǣdan}} (English {{m|en|read}}), Old Saxon {{m|osx|rādan}} (Low German {{m|nds|raden}}) Old Dutch {{m|odt|rādan}} (Dutch {{m|nl|raden}}), Old High German {{m|goh|rātan}} (German {{m|de|raten}}), Gothic {{m|got|𐌲𐌰𐍂𐌴𐌳𐌰𐌽|tr=garedan}}, which is akin to Gothic {{m|got|𐍂𐍉𐌳𐌾𐌰𐌽||to talk together|tr=rodjan}} <ref>[http://ordnet.dk/ods/search?id=524991 Etymology of the verb in] [[:w:da:ODS|ODS]]</ref>. The Indo-European root is also the source of Greek {{m|el|αριθμός|sc=Grek}}, Old Irish {{m|sga|immrádim}}, Old Church Slavonic {{m|cu|радити|sc=Cyrs|tr=raditi}}, Albanian {{m|sq|re||care, attention}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/rauːð/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|auːð|lang=is}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|n|ráðs|ráð}}

# [[advice]], [[counsel]]
# [[plan]]
# [[council]] {{gloss|body of advisors}}

